209
00:07:41,933 --> 00:07:42,567
YES.

210
00:07:42,567 --> 00:07:43,568
WEATHER GIRLS TODAY.

211
00:07:43,568 --> 00:07:45,670
LOOK AT MISS J.
THE PARK RANGER.

212
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:47,572
THE REASON WHY I WANTED
YOU GUYS TO COME HERE TODAY

213
00:07:47,572 --> 00:07:51,276
IS BECAUSE FOR MY VERY FIRST
FASHION SHOW IN LOS ANGELES,

214
00:07:51,276 --> 00:07:52,243
THE DESIGNERS
ARE LIKE...

215
00:07:52,243 --> 00:07:54,212
(foreign accent)
"TYRA, I WANT YOU TO GET
ON THE STAGE,

216
00:07:54,212 --> 00:07:55,914
AND I WANT YOU
TO LOOK LIKE A CAT."

217
00:07:55,914 --> 00:07:58,283
(normal voice)
SO I GET ON THE RUNWAY
AND I'M, LIKE, WALKING,

218
00:07:58,283 --> 00:08:00,218
AND I GET TO THE END
AND I AM LIKE, "MEOW."

219
00:08:00,218 --> 00:08:01,786
(hisses)

220
00:08:01,786 --> 00:08:03,421
AND I WENT BACKSTAGE,
AND THE DESIGNER WAS LIKE...

221
00:08:03,421 --> 00:08:05,190
(foreign accent)
"YOU HAVE RUINED MY SHOW.
WHAT WAS THAT MOVE?

222
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:06,591
I DON'T KNOW WHAT YOU DID."

223
00:08:06,591 --> 00:08:10,395
(normal voice)
SO I REALIZED THAT HE MEANT
TO BE FELINE-LIKE.

224
00:08:10,395 --> 00:08:13,198
WHEN YOU DO MODELING JOBS,
A PHOTOGRAPHER WILL TELL YOU,

225
00:08:13,198 --> 00:08:15,333
"I WANT YOU TO BE LIKE A BIRD,
I WANT YOU TO BE LIKE A CAT.

226
00:08:15,333 --> 00:08:16,734
I WANT YOU TO BE LIKE
A RHINOCEROS."

227
00:08:16,734 --> 00:08:18,169
YOU CAN LEARN HOW
TO DO IT EXACTLY

228
00:08:18,169 --> 00:08:21,372
AND THEN KIND OF MOLD IT
INTO YOUR OWN THING.

229
00:08:21,372 --> 00:08:23,174
YOU GUYS ARE DOING
A SPECIAL PHOTO SHOOT TODAY.

230
00:08:23,174 --> 00:08:24,275
IT'S AN AMAZING SHOOT

231
00:08:24,275 --> 00:08:26,377
BECAUSE YOU GUYS NEED MODELS
WITH YOU!

232
00:08:26,377 --> 00:08:27,278
WHOO!

233
00:08:27,278 --> 00:08:29,113
THESE ARE YOUR MODELS TODAY.

234
00:08:29,113 --> 00:08:30,048
OH, WOW.

235
00:08:30,048 --> 00:08:31,015
ARE YOU READY?

236
00:08:31,883 --> 00:08:32,984
THEY'RE NO JOKE.

237
00:08:32,984 --> 00:08:35,086
YOU SEE, THEY'RE TRYING
TO GET AT YOU RIGHT NOW.

238
00:08:35,086 --> 00:08:36,087
WHAT?

239
00:08:36,087 --> 00:08:37,589
YEAH. THIS IS--I DON'T KNOW.

240
00:08:37,589 --> 00:08:39,324
YOU THINK THEY CAN DO
THE SHOOT TODAY?

241
00:08:39,324 --> 00:08:40,425
I MEAN, WE MANAGED--

242
00:08:40,425 --> 00:08:41,693
WE DID IT ALL MORNING LONG.

243
00:08:41,693 --> 00:08:42,460
I DON'T KNOW.

244
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:44,962
I'M COLD,
AND I'M NOT FEELIN' THE RAIN,

245
00:08:44,962 --> 00:08:46,297
I'M NOT FEELING
THIS WEATHER.

246
00:08:46,297 --> 00:08:48,533
AND... I THINK Y'ALL

247
00:08:48,533 --> 00:08:50,635
ARE GONNA HAVE DO
THIS SHOOT IN AFRICA!

248
00:08:50,635 --> 00:08:53,671
(screaming)

249
00:08:53,671 --> 00:08:54,505
OH, MY GOD!

250
00:08:54,505 --> 00:08:56,040
OH, MY GOD!

251
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:58,409
YOU GUYS, WE'RE GOING
TO SOUTH AFRICA.

252
00:08:58,409 --> 00:08:59,077
WOW.

253
00:08:59,077 --> 00:09:00,745
BUT YOU GUYS
HAVE TO PACK TONIGHT.

254
00:09:00,745 --> 00:09:01,479
ARE YOU READY?

255
00:09:01,479 --> 00:09:02,447
YES!

256
00:09:02,447 --> 00:09:03,414
ALL RIGHTY.

257
00:09:03,414 --> 00:09:04,415
LET'S DO IT.

258
00:09:04,415 --> 00:09:06,351
WHOO!

259
00:09:06,351 --> 00:09:08,553
LET'S GO TO AFRICA!

260
00:09:08,553 --> 00:09:10,121
SOUTH AFRICA!

261
00:09:10,121 --> 00:09:11,522
WHOO!

262
00:09:15,727 --> 00:09:17,528
♪♪♪

263
00:09:17,528 --> 00:09:18,930
KEENYAH, HERE'S YOUR DRESS.

264
00:09:18,930 --> 00:09:20,098
I GONNA
JUST DUMP EVERYTHING OUT

265
00:09:20,098 --> 00:09:20,698
AND START OVER.

266
00:09:20,698 --> 00:09:22,033
WE ARE GOING TO AFRICA.

267
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:25,270
WE HAVE TWO HOURS TO PACK,
HAVE TO BRING EVERYTHING.

268
00:09:25,270 --> 00:09:28,006
DO NOT LEAVE A SOCK
IF YOU WANT THAT SOCK BACK.

269
00:09:28,006 --> 00:09:29,574
IS THAT ACTUALLY WORKING?

270
00:09:29,574 --> 00:09:30,642
I THINK SO.

271
00:09:30,642 --> 00:09:32,043
ONCE WE GET TO AFRICA,

272
00:09:32,043 --> 00:09:34,312
THE COMPETITION IS GONNA BE
OUT OF THIS WORLD.

273
00:09:34,312 --> 00:09:35,146
ANYTHING CAN HAPPEN,

274
00:09:35,146 --> 00:09:36,948
AND WE'LL HAVE TO KEEP
OUR EYES ON THE PRIZE.

275
00:09:40,184 --> 00:09:41,686
GOOD-BYE, L.A.

276
00:09:45,890 --> 00:09:52,964
♪♪♪

277
00:09:52,964 --> 00:09:59,771
(singing in African language)

278
00:10:11,649 --> 00:10:13,451
IT'S, LIKE,
A REALLY LONG FLIGHT,

279
00:10:13,451 --> 00:10:15,153
AND THEN
WHEN WE FINALLY GET HERE,

280
00:10:15,153 --> 00:10:16,287
IT'S BEAUTIFUL.

281
00:10:16,287 --> 00:10:18,790
WE SEE MOUNTAINS
AND IT'S SUNNY AND IT'S HOT.

282
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:20,091
WE HAVE TO WALK LIKE THIS.

283
00:10:21,125 --> 00:10:22,026
WE'RE LIKE, OH, MY GOSH,

284
00:10:22,026 --> 00:10:23,328
WE CAN'T BELIEVE
WE'RE IN AFRICA.

285
00:10:23,328 --> 00:10:24,028
CAN YOU BELIEVE IT?

286
00:10:24,028 --> 00:10:26,297
WE'RE ON AFRICAN DIRT.
LIKE, IT'S CRAZY.

287
00:10:30,968 --> 00:10:34,172
BRITTANY AND KEENYAH JOKE
ALL THE TIME.

288
00:10:34,172 --> 00:10:36,307
I AM NOT USED TO OPENING UP
TO PEOPLE,

289
00:10:36,307 --> 00:10:38,476
AND I HAVE BEEN TRYING TO
CONNECT WITH THEM MORE.

290
00:10:38,476 --> 00:10:39,677
BUT I'M PART OF THE GROUP,

291
00:10:39,677 --> 00:10:41,879
BUT NOT, LIKE,
A MAJOR PART OF THE GROUP.

292
00:10:41,879 --> 00:10:42,747
DID YOU READ THE PACKET?

293
00:10:42,747 --> 00:10:44,482
IT SAID WHEN YOU'RE
IN CONVERSATION,

294
00:10:44,482 --> 00:10:46,317
DON'T PUT YOUR HANDS
IN YOUR POCKET,

295
00:10:46,317 --> 00:10:47,185
BECAUSE THAT'S RUDE.

296
00:10:47,185 --> 00:10:48,086
LOOK THEM IN THE EYE

297
00:10:48,086 --> 00:10:50,455
AND DON'T POINT
WITH YOUR INDEX FINGER.

298
00:10:50,455 --> 00:10:51,756
REALLY?

299
00:10:51,756 --> 00:10:54,325
WELL, THAT'S THE SAME RULE
AS IN AMERICA,

300
00:10:54,325 --> 00:10:55,460
IT'S JUST NOT WRITTEN DOWN.

301
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:56,461
SO THIS IS NOT GOOD?

302
00:10:56,461 --> 00:10:58,296
WE CAN'T DO THAT
IN AMERICA EITHER.

303
00:10:58,296 --> 00:11:01,199
I FEEL LIKE BRITTANY
AND KEENYAH JUST JOKE,

304
00:11:01,199 --> 00:11:02,967
BECAUSE, YOU KNOW,
EVERY TIME I SAY SOMETHING,

305
00:11:02,967 --> 00:11:04,135
IT'S LIKE,
"OH, THAT'S FUNNY.

306
00:11:04,135 --> 00:11:05,370
LET'S MAKE FUN OF IT."

307
00:11:05,370 --> 00:11:07,338
SOMETIMES YOU GET
REALLY TIRED OF THAT.

308
00:11:08,806 --> 00:11:10,875
WE ARE IN CAPE TOWN.

309
00:11:10,875 --> 00:11:13,778
WE NEED, LIKE, AFRICAN MUSIC,
SOME DRUM BEATS, SOMETHING.

310
00:11:13,778 --> 00:11:18,316
(humming)

311
00:11:21,786 --> 00:11:29,727
♪♪♪

312
00:11:38,403 --> 00:11:40,438
I STILL CAN'T BELIEVE
WE'RE HERE IN SOUTH AFRICA,

313
00:11:40,438 --> 00:11:42,073
BUT WHERE ARE WE GOING?

314
00:11:44,675 --> 00:11:45,943
GOOD AFTERNOON, LADIES.

315
00:11:45,943 --> 00:11:47,111
WELCOME TO AQUILA.

316
00:11:47,111 --> 00:11:48,446
WELCOME TO SOUTH AFRICA.

317
00:11:48,446 --> 00:11:50,415
I'M PIERRE,
THE MANAGER AT THE RESERVE.

318
00:11:50,415 --> 00:11:51,449
FOLLOW ME.
THANK YOU.

319
00:11:55,553 --> 00:11:57,088
WE SEE THE DRUMMERS
IN THE DISTANCE, AND I WENT,

320
00:11:57,088 --> 00:11:58,790
LIKE, "YEAH, THIS IS TOUGH,
THIS IS HIP."

321
00:11:58,790 --> 00:12:02,527
THIS IS JUST A TASTE OF WHAT
SOUTH AFRICA HAS TO OFFER.

322
00:12:07,532 --> 00:12:08,599
OH!

323
00:12:08,599 --> 00:12:09,834
AAH!

324
00:12:09,834 --> 00:12:11,969
ALL OF A SUDDEN
TYRA RUNS IN BEHIND US,

325
00:12:11,969 --> 00:12:13,838
AND WE'RE LIKE,
"OH, TYRA--SHE'S HERE!"

326
00:12:13,838 --> 00:12:16,207
LIKE, SHE ALWAYS POPS UP
AT, LIKE, THE WEIRDEST TIMES.

327
00:12:18,042 --> 00:12:19,243
HI!

328
00:12:19,243 --> 00:12:20,478
HI, TYRA!

329
00:12:20,478 --> 00:12:22,413
WELCOME TO SOUTH AFRICA!

330
00:12:22,413 --> 00:12:23,648
ISN'T IT BEAUTIFUL?

331
00:12:23,648 --> 00:12:25,082
YES.

332
00:12:25,082 --> 00:12:25,850
SO LET ME TELL YOU

333
00:12:25,850 --> 00:12:27,585
A LITTLE BIT
ABOUT WHY YOU'RE HERE.

334
00:12:27,585 --> 00:12:29,520
IN SOUTH AFRICA,
FASHION WEEK IS HUGE.

335
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:31,422
THEY HAVE
AFRICAN-TYPE DESIGNERS,

336
00:12:31,422 --> 00:12:33,057
YOU KNOW, FOR, LIKE,
THE TRADITIONAL GARB,

337
00:12:33,057 --> 00:12:34,158
ALL THE WAY TO HAUTE COUTURE.

338
00:12:34,158 --> 00:12:35,760
THIS IS NOW
A PLACE FOR NEW MODELS

339
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:36,694
TO COME TO MAKE IT.

340
00:12:36,694 --> 00:12:38,596
I HAD MY VERY FIRST COVER
OF "SPORTS ILLUSTRATED"

341
00:12:38,596 --> 00:12:39,797
SHOT HERE IN SOUTH AFRICA.

342
00:12:39,797 --> 00:12:41,899
THEY HAVE
SOUTH AFRICAN "COSMOPOLITAN,"

343
00:12:41,899 --> 00:12:44,535
SOUTH AFRICAN "ELLE,"
AND THEIR OWN LOCAL MAGAZINES.

344
00:12:44,535 --> 00:12:47,238
NONE OF US GIRLS
HAD ANY IDEA THAT SOUTH AFRICA

345
00:12:47,238 --> 00:12:51,709
WAS DEVELOPING ITSELF IN
THE FASHION INDUSTRY WHATSOEVER.

346
00:12:51,709 --> 00:12:52,610
OH, MY GOD.

347
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:54,245
WHEN THE HELL DID THIS HAPPEN?

348
00:12:54,245 --> 00:12:57,415
SO YOU GUYS ARE GONNA BE
EXPERIENCING A LOT HERE,

349
00:12:57,415 --> 00:12:59,817
AND HOPEFULLY HAVING
LOTS OF PICTURES TO TAKE HOME.

350
00:12:59,817 --> 00:13:01,486
SO CAN WE GET
A LITTLE GROOVE ON?

351
00:13:01,486 --> 00:13:02,453
YEAH!

352
00:13:02,453 --> 00:13:10,394
♪♪♪

353
00:13:13,231 --> 00:13:14,732
THESE DANCERS
COME RUNNING OUT

354
00:13:14,732 --> 00:13:16,801
IN THEIR LITTLE
CHEETAH OUTFITS.

355
00:13:16,801 --> 00:13:19,270
I DON'T KNOW
WHAT THE HELL IS GOING ON.

356
00:13:19,270 --> 00:13:20,972
AAH!

357
00:13:20,972 --> 00:13:22,640
I FELT LIKE
IT WAS A SHARK FRENZY.

358
00:13:22,640 --> 00:13:24,675
THEY'RE SLOWLY
CIRCLING AROUND US,

359
00:13:24,675 --> 00:13:26,911
TYRA GRABS MY HAND
AND THROWS ME IN THE LINE.

360
00:13:26,911 --> 00:13:28,813
I'M, LIKE, "OKAY, FINE,
I'LL DO IT.

361
00:13:28,813 --> 00:13:36,754
♪♪♪

362
00:13:38,356 --> 00:13:39,657
BYE.

363
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:51,002
NEXT THING I KNOW,
TYRA'S JUST MISSING.

364
00:13:51,002 --> 00:13:52,970
TYRA JUST KIND OF CREEPS OUT.

365
00:13:52,970 --> 00:13:54,171
"BYE, GIRLS."

366
00:13:54,171 --> 00:13:55,706
SHE'S OUT. QUICKNESS.

367
00:13:58,009 --> 00:13:58,943
GOOD AFTERNOON, LADIES.

368
00:13:58,943 --> 00:14:00,645
WE'RE GOING TO TAKE YOU
ON A LITTLE SAFARI.

369
00:14:00,645 --> 00:14:01,612
ALL RIGHT.

370
00:14:01,612 --> 00:14:02,313
OH, YEAH.

371
00:14:02,313 --> 00:14:04,782
PIERRE TELLS US WE'RE GOING
ON A SAFARI,

372
00:14:04,782 --> 00:14:06,717
AND I AM GOING THROUGH
THE ROOF.

373
00:14:06,717 --> 00:14:08,886
I AM DEFINITELY
LOOKING FORWARD TO THIS.

374
00:14:13,291 --> 00:14:14,825
ALL RIGHT. THANK YOU.

375
00:14:16,327 --> 00:14:17,628
HIPPO IN THE WATER,
EVERYBODY.

376
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:18,296
HIPPO!

377
00:14:18,296 --> 00:14:19,163
OH, I DO SEE HIM.

378
00:14:19,163 --> 00:14:21,232
OOH! HE'S LOOKING
FOR MARBLES.

379
00:14:21,232 --> 00:14:23,634
DO YOU KNOW HOW MANY TONS
THEY WEIGH?

380
00:14:23,634 --> 00:14:24,368
NO. 2?

381
00:14:24,368 --> 00:14:24,969
NO. HOW MANY?

382
00:14:24,969 --> 00:14:26,237
ABOUT 1 1/2 TONS.

383
00:14:26,237 --> 00:14:27,104
WOW.

384
00:14:27,104 --> 00:14:28,205
SAME AMOUNT AS KEENYAH.

385
00:14:28,205 --> 00:14:29,840
OH HO!

386
00:14:29,840 --> 00:14:30,808
I'M JUST KIDDING.

387
00:14:30,808 --> 00:14:31,909
GLUTTONY!

388
00:14:31,909 --> 00:14:33,644
KEENYAH'S GLUTTONY
PHOTO SHOOT,

389
00:14:33,644 --> 00:14:35,846
SHE MAKES A JOKE OUT OF IT,
WHICH IS GREAT.

390
00:14:35,846 --> 00:14:37,048
IT'S HILARIOUS.

391
00:14:37,048 --> 00:14:38,516
I DON'T WANNA FALL OUT

392
00:14:38,516 --> 00:14:40,217
OR THE HIPPO IS GONNA EAT ME
FOR LUNCH.

393
00:14:40,217 --> 00:14:42,787
THE THING ABOUT MY WEIGHT,
I FEEL LIKE I CAN STILL DO THIS

394
00:14:42,787 --> 00:14:44,822
BECAUSE YOANNA
HAD PROBLEMS WITH HER WEIGHT,

395
00:14:44,822 --> 00:14:46,657
AND SHE ENDED UP WINNING
THE COMPETITION.

396
00:14:46,657 --> 00:14:48,526
I DON'T APPROVE
OF THIS CONVERSATION

397
00:14:48,526 --> 00:14:49,627
BECAUSE I'M NOT IN IT.

398
00:14:49,627 --> 00:14:51,596
♪ THE BRITTANY SHOW ♪♪

399
00:14:51,596 --> 00:14:52,964
LOOK AT HOW BEAUTIFUL
THAT LOOKS.

400
00:14:52,964 --> 00:14:53,764
GIRAFFE.

401
00:14:53,764 --> 00:14:55,232
IT'S A MOM AND HER DAUGHTER.

402
00:14:55,232 --> 00:14:55,700
WHERE?

403
00:14:55,700 --> 00:14:56,534
WHERE ARE THEY?

404
00:14:56,534 --> 00:14:59,737
AND I'LL TELL YOU THE QUESTION--
CAN I RIDE ONE OF 'EM?

405
00:14:59,737 --> 00:15:01,305
CAN I RUN OUT THERE
WITH THE BUFFALO?

406
00:15:01,305 --> 00:15:02,440
CAN YOU GRAZE WITH THEM?

407
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:03,240
YOU GO RIGHT AHEAD,
BRITTANY.

408
00:15:03,240 --> 00:15:04,775
THAT'S WHAT KILLED MUFASA.

409
00:15:06,143 --> 00:15:07,278
HOLY SHIMOLYS!

410
00:15:07,278 --> 00:15:08,212
LOOK AT THOSE RHINOS.

411
00:15:08,212 --> 00:15:09,780
RHINOS! WE'VE GOT RHINOS.

412
00:15:09,780 --> 00:15:10,815
OH, LOOK AT 'EM.

413
00:15:10,815 --> 00:15:11,949
LOOK AT 'EM.

414
00:15:13,618 --> 00:15:14,885
ARE THOSE ALL SPRINGBOKS?

415
00:15:14,885 --> 00:15:16,053
THEY'RE ALL SPRINGBOKS.

416
00:15:16,053 --> 00:15:17,521
GOSH.

417
00:15:17,521 --> 00:15:19,590
A LOT OF THE ANIMALS
ON THE SAFARI,

418
00:15:19,590 --> 00:15:21,993
THEY JUST SAT THERE, CHILLED.

419
00:15:21,993 --> 00:15:23,561
I WANTED TO SEE SOME ACTION.

420
00:15:32,703 --> 00:15:34,305
HAVE THERE BEEN ANY ATTACKS?

421
00:15:34,305 --> 00:15:35,172
NOT YET.

422
00:15:35,172 --> 00:15:36,307
NOT YET.

423
00:15:36,307 --> 00:15:38,142
WE'RE ABOUT TO ENTER
THE LION ZONE,

424
00:15:38,142 --> 00:15:40,144
AND WE CAN'T MAKE ANY NOISE.

425
00:15:40,144 --> 00:15:42,713
AND WE ALL AUTOMATICALLY
LOOK TO BRITTANY.

426
00:15:42,713 --> 00:15:43,714
WHAT ARE YOU LOOKING AT?

427
00:15:43,714 --> 00:15:44,215
WHAT?

428
00:15:44,215 --> 00:15:46,450
THEY KNOW SOMEBODY'S
GONNA SAY SOMETHING.

429
00:15:46,450 --> 00:15:47,218
ABOUT WHAT?

430
00:15:47,218 --> 00:15:49,920
ONCE IT GETS EYE CONTACT
WITH BRITTANY, I'M OUTTA HERE.

431
00:15:49,920 --> 00:15:51,522
I AM OUT OF HERE.

432
00:15:51,522 --> 00:15:53,024
I'LL BE BEATING 'EM DOWN.

433
00:15:54,258 --> 00:15:56,494
I AM NOT GETTING ATTACKED
BEFORE ELIMINATION

434
00:15:56,494 --> 00:15:57,328
BECAUSE OF BRITTANY.

435
00:15:57,328 --> 00:15:59,063
I AM NOT. I REFUSE TO.

436
00:16:01,432 --> 00:16:03,401
SO IF WE'RE RUNNING AWAY
FROM A LION,

437
00:16:03,401 --> 00:16:04,869
AND WE GET ATTACKED,
THERE'S NO WAY OUT?

438
00:16:04,869 --> 00:16:05,336
EXACTLY.

439
00:16:05,336 --> 00:16:06,404
RIGHT.

440
00:16:06,404 --> 00:16:07,571
DO WE HAVE TO BE QUIET NOW?

441
00:16:07,571 --> 00:16:08,472
PARDON ME?

442
00:16:08,472 --> 00:16:09,540
DO WE HAVE TO BE QUIET?

443
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:10,574
YES.

444
00:16:21,919 --> 00:16:23,187
OH, MY GOD!

445
00:16:25,723 --> 00:16:27,291
I'M LIKE, "OKAY."

446
00:16:27,291 --> 00:16:28,459
WE WERE REALLY ON A SAFARI,

447
00:16:28,459 --> 00:16:30,127
BUT, JEEZ, LIKE, THE LIONS
COULD ATTACK US.

448
00:16:30,127 --> 00:16:31,862
THERE'S NOTHING
BLOCKING THEM FROM US

449
00:16:31,862 --> 00:16:34,298
IF THEY WANTED
TO HAVE US FOR DINNER.

450
00:16:34,298 --> 00:16:36,534
I CAN'T SING OR DANCE
RIGHT NOW?

451
00:16:36,534 --> 00:16:37,134
SHH.

452
00:16:37,134 --> 00:16:39,470
IS THERE NO SINGING
AND DANCING PAST THIS POINT?

453
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:40,504
(whispers)
BRITTANY, STOP.

454
00:16:40,504 --> 00:16:41,205
THEY'RE GETTING UP.

455
00:16:41,205 --> 00:16:42,173
OH, THEY'RE GETTING UP.

456
00:16:42,173 --> 00:16:43,874
WE'RE EYEING THEM,
AREN'T WE?

457
00:16:46,444 --> 00:16:47,945
(engine revs)

458
00:16:47,945 --> 00:16:49,480
(horn honks)

459
00:16:52,950 --> 00:16:53,951
OH, MY GOD.

460
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,821
OH, MY GOD.

461
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:11,501
WE'RE EYING THEM,
AREN'T WE?

462
00:17:13,404 --> 00:17:14,204
(whispers)
WHY ARE YOU--

463
00:17:14,204 --> 00:17:15,271
RAWR.

464
00:17:15,271 --> 00:17:17,040
THE LIONS,
THEY'RE VERY DANGEROUS.

465
00:17:17,040 --> 00:17:18,675
BE VERY, VERY QUIET,

466
00:17:18,675 --> 00:17:20,211
DON'T MAKE
ANY SUDDEN MOVEMENTS,

467
00:17:20,211 --> 00:17:21,412
AND BRITTANY
IS NOT AFRAID OF THIS.

468
00:17:21,412 --> 00:17:22,413
I HAVE NO IDEA WHY.

469
00:17:22,413 --> 00:17:24,080
WE ARE LIKE,
"BRITTANY, SHUT UP!"

470
00:17:25,549 --> 00:17:27,084
(engine revs)

471
00:17:27,084 --> 00:17:28,452
(horn honks)

472
00:17:31,822 --> 00:17:32,790
OH, MY GOD.

473
00:17:34,558 --> 00:17:35,693
OH, MY GOD.

474
00:17:47,805 --> 00:17:49,240
OH, MY GOD.

475
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:51,675
OH, MY GOD. NEVER AGAIN.

476
00:17:51,675 --> 00:17:52,943
IT WAS BRITTANY'S FAULT.

477
00:17:53,811 --> 00:17:55,045
I WANNA GO BACK
AND DO THAT AGAIN.

478
00:17:55,045 --> 00:17:56,647
I COULD HAVE SWORN
WE WERE ABOUT TO GET ATTACKED.

479
00:17:56,647 --> 00:17:57,615
SHE WAS LIKE...

480
00:17:57,615 --> 00:17:58,916
OH, NO. OH, NO.

481
00:18:01,418 --> 00:18:05,189
♪♪♪

482
00:18:05,189 --> 00:18:07,725
SO WE'RE DRIVING ALONG,
AND IT'S GETTING REALLY DARK.

483
00:18:07,725 --> 00:18:09,693
WE SEE A FIRE,
AND WE'RE ALL THINKING,

484
00:18:09,693 --> 00:18:11,829
"OH, GOD, MAYBE THIS
IS A PHOTO SHOOT."

485
00:18:11,829 --> 00:18:12,930
WE HAVE NO IDEA.

486
00:18:14,265 --> 00:18:17,034
I UNDERSTAND THAT
THERE HAS BEEN SOME CHALLENGE.

487
00:18:17,034 --> 00:18:18,068
AND WHO IS THE WINNER?

488
00:18:18,068 --> 00:18:19,603
ME!

489
00:18:19,603 --> 00:18:20,638
AND WHO DID YOU PICK?

490
00:18:20,638 --> 00:18:21,505
THESE TWO.

491
00:18:21,505 --> 00:18:23,040
OKAY, CONGRATULATIONS, GUYS.

492
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:24,508
WE'RE STAYING
OUT HERE.
THANK YOU.

493
00:18:24,508 --> 00:18:26,177
YOU ARE GOING BACK WITH ME.

494
00:18:26,177 --> 00:18:28,479
YOU ARE GOING TO STAY IN ONE
OF OUR LUXURY ACCOMMODATIONS.

495
00:18:28,479 --> 00:18:29,814
AND THE OTHER GUYS--

496
00:18:29,814 --> 00:18:31,816
THEY ARE GOING
TO STAY RIGHT HERE.

497
00:18:31,816 --> 00:18:33,517
WHOO!

498
00:18:33,517 --> 00:18:35,820
BUT YOU HAVE TO BUILD
YOUR OWN TENT.

499
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:36,387
OOH.

500
00:18:36,387 --> 00:18:38,455
I HAVE TO BUILD
MY OWN TENT?

501
00:18:38,455 --> 00:18:39,356
WOW.

502
00:18:39,356 --> 00:18:42,026
OKAY, UM,
IS THIS THAT OUR TENT?

503
00:18:42,026 --> 00:18:44,728
THANK GOD
I WATCHED "SURVIVOR."

504
00:18:44,728 --> 00:18:46,530
HOW LONG AM I GONNA BE
OUT HERE?

505
00:18:46,530 --> 00:18:48,566
I HAVE NEVER GONE CAMPING.

506
00:18:48,566 --> 00:18:50,734
ALL THESE QUESTIONS START
GOING THROUGH MY HEAD LIKE,

507
00:18:50,734 --> 00:18:53,337
UM, BLOW DRYER, HOT IRON.

508
00:18:53,337 --> 00:18:54,805
MY HAIR IS GONNA FRIZZ.

509
00:18:54,805 --> 00:18:56,307
WE LOVE YOU GIRLS,
BUT WE GOTTA GO.

510
00:18:56,307 --> 00:18:57,741
GOOD NIGHT.

511
00:18:57,741 --> 00:19:00,644
SO, LADIES, LET'S START
BUILDING OUR SHELTER.

512
00:19:00,644 --> 00:19:02,746
MICHELLE'S ALWAYS, LIKE,
"THIS IS GONNA BE AWESOME,"

513
00:19:02,746 --> 00:19:04,815
AND I APPRECIATE
THAT QUALITY IN HER,

514
00:19:04,815 --> 00:19:06,884
BUT I THINK A LOT OF THAT

515
00:19:06,884 --> 00:19:11,388
IS HER WANTING TO APPEAR
STRONG TO OTHER PEOPLE.

516
00:19:11,388 --> 00:19:12,957
OH, THIS ISN'T
GONNA BE THAT BAD.

517
00:19:12,957 --> 00:19:15,659
OH! OH, MY GOD. OH!

518
00:19:15,659 --> 00:19:17,061
THAT WAS, LIKE, A ROACH
OR SOMETHING.

519
00:19:17,061 --> 00:19:18,128
I DON'T KNOW.

520
00:19:18,128 --> 00:19:20,664
(laughing)

521
00:19:25,102 --> 00:19:26,837
THAT IS NOT FUNNY.

522
00:19:26,837 --> 00:19:27,905
BYE, GIRLS.

523
00:19:27,905 --> 00:19:29,106
BYE.

524
00:19:29,807 --> 00:19:31,609
LOVE YOU, KAHLEN.

525
00:19:31,609 --> 00:19:33,143
LOVE YOU, NAIMA.

526
00:19:34,879 --> 00:19:36,947
LOVE YOU, MICHELLE.

527
00:19:41,385 --> 00:19:42,553
WELCOME, LADIES.

528
00:19:42,553 --> 00:19:43,520
WOW.

529
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:44,889
HERE'S YOUR ROOM
FOR THE EVENING.

530
00:19:46,090 --> 00:19:49,159
TO A LUXURIOUS NIGHT
IN AFRICA.

531
00:19:49,159 --> 00:19:50,227
LET'S SAY IT TOGETHER.

532
00:19:50,227 --> 00:19:52,796
IN AFRICA.

533
00:19:52,796 --> 00:19:54,932
WE ARE NOT
OUT IN THE WILDERNESS.

534
00:19:54,932 --> 00:19:55,799
CHEERS TO THAT.

535
00:19:55,799 --> 00:19:56,734
CHEERS TO THAT.

536
00:19:56,734 --> 00:19:59,436
HOW MANY MODELS DOES IT TAKE
TO PEE IN THE WILDERNESS?

537
00:19:59,436 --> 00:20:00,271
TWO?

538
00:20:00,271 --> 00:20:03,140
CAN YOU GET ME
SOME TOILET PAPER?

539
00:20:03,140 --> 00:20:05,542
THERE IS NO WAY
THAT MY ANCESTORS DID THIS.

540
00:20:05,542 --> 00:20:08,345
IT'S A GOOD THING THAT
THE HIGH-MAINTENANCE GIRLS

541
00:20:08,345 --> 00:20:10,247
GET TO STAY
IN THE 5-STAR HOTEL,

542
00:20:10,247 --> 00:20:12,750
BECAUSE THEY NEVER
WOULD HAVE SURVIVED.

543
00:20:12,750 --> 00:20:14,151
I WONDER WHAT
THE OTHER GIRLS ARE DOING.

544
00:20:14,151 --> 00:20:16,887
OH, EATING STRAWBERRIES
AND CHOCOLATE, CHAMPAGNE--

545
00:20:16,887 --> 00:20:18,389
IN THE JACUZZI.

546
00:20:18,389 --> 00:20:20,991
THERE'S ROSE PETALS
IN THE HOT TUB.

547
00:20:20,991 --> 00:20:23,060
OH, AND LITTLE FRIENDS.

548
00:20:23,060 --> 00:20:24,595
LITTLE FRIENDS
AREN'T STILL ALIVE.

549
00:20:26,063 --> 00:20:27,097
AAH!

550
00:20:27,097 --> 00:20:28,399
OH, GROSS.

551
00:20:28,399 --> 00:20:30,534
OH! OKAY, I'M DONE.

552
00:20:30,534 --> 00:20:32,169
NATURE MEETS BEVERLY HILLS.

553
00:20:32,169 --> 00:20:33,837
I JUST DON'T LIKE BUGS
VERY MUCH.

554
00:20:33,837 --> 00:20:35,673
I CAN'T TAKE THESE BUGS.

555
00:20:35,673 --> 00:20:36,707
AAH!

556
00:20:36,707 --> 00:20:38,342
WE'RE BEING TORTURED!

557
00:20:38,342 --> 00:20:39,410
(laughs)

558
00:20:39,410 --> 00:20:40,644
THIS IS NOT A VACATION.

559
00:20:40,644 --> 00:20:41,612
WE'RE REALLY ROUGHING IT.

560
00:20:41,612 --> 00:20:43,047
OH, GET OUT OF THE BED.

561
00:20:44,048 --> 00:20:45,282
GET, GET.

562
00:20:45,282 --> 00:20:46,283
AAH!

563
00:20:46,283 --> 00:20:47,885
OH! GET OUT OF HERE!

564
00:20:47,885 --> 00:20:48,953
OH, THERE'S A COCKROACH!

565
00:20:48,953 --> 00:20:49,887
ON YOUR PILLOW?

566
00:20:49,887 --> 00:20:50,888
WHAT THE HELL?

567
00:20:50,888 --> 00:20:51,855
ARE YOU JOKING?

568
00:20:51,855 --> 00:20:53,090
YOU KNOW,
IF WE ARE GETTING EATEN UP,

569
00:20:53,090 --> 00:20:55,225
I DON'T EVEN KNOW
HOW THE OTHER GIRLS ARE.

570
00:20:55,225 --> 00:21:00,597
♪♪♪

571
00:21:00,597 --> 00:21:01,598
IS THAT A SNAKE?

572
00:21:01,598 --> 00:21:03,434
OH! OH!

573
00:21:03,434 --> 00:21:04,868
(laughing)

574
00:21:04,868 --> 00:21:06,904
THAT SCARED ME SO MUCH.

575
00:21:09,306 --> 00:21:10,374
GOOD MORNING.

576
00:21:10,374 --> 00:21:11,342
GOOD MORNING, LADIES.

577
00:21:11,342 --> 00:21:12,176
WELCOME BACK.

578
00:21:12,176 --> 00:21:13,377
THERE'S A NICE,
HOT BREAKFAST

579
00:21:13,377 --> 00:21:14,712
WAITING FOR YOU
IN THE RESTAURANT.

580
00:21:14,712 --> 00:21:16,613
OH, I LOVE YOU!

581
00:21:16,613 --> 00:21:17,247
THANK YOU.

582
00:21:17,247 --> 00:21:17,748
ALL RIGHT.

583
00:21:17,748 --> 00:21:18,782
WELL, HEY THERE, LADIES.

584
00:21:18,782 --> 00:21:19,750
HOW WAS YOUR NIGHT?

585
00:21:19,750 --> 00:21:20,517
IT WAS ROUGH.

586
00:21:20,517 --> 00:21:21,752
THANK YOU.

587
00:21:26,590 --> 00:21:28,192
THAT'S A LOT.
CAN YOU TELL?

588
00:21:28,192 --> 00:21:29,193
NO.
A LITTLE BIT?

589
00:21:30,194 --> 00:21:31,695
WHEN I'M UNDER
A LOT OF STRESS,

590
00:21:31,695 --> 00:21:33,664
I FIND A REAL COMFORT
IN EATING.

591
00:21:33,664 --> 00:21:35,866
KEENYAH--SHE FEELS LIKE
SHE GAINING SOME WEIGHT,

592
00:21:35,866 --> 00:21:37,901
BUT WHEN THE NEXT BREAD TRAY
COMES AROUND,

593
00:21:37,901 --> 00:21:40,471
SHE'LL BE THE FIRST ONE TO GRAB
A CROISSANT OR TWO OFF OF IT.

594
00:21:40,471 --> 00:21:42,206
I THINK I'D LIKE
A BOWL OF THAT YOGURT.

595
00:21:42,206 --> 00:21:44,141
KEENYAH--
JUST FILLING UP MORE.

596
00:21:44,141 --> 00:21:45,542
IT'S JUST YOGURT.

597
00:21:45,542 --> 00:21:47,044
SHE SAYS SHE WANTS
TO LOSE WEIGHT

598
00:21:47,044 --> 00:21:47,878
AND SHE WANTS HELP.

599
00:21:47,878 --> 00:21:50,180
WELL, IF I'M GONNA HELP,
SHE'S GETTIN' RIBBED.

600
00:21:50,180 --> 00:21:51,215
YOGURT!

601
00:21:53,884 --> 00:21:55,853
OH, LOOK WHO IT IS.

602
00:21:55,853 --> 00:21:57,621
HEY, GIRLS, COME OVER HERE.

603
00:21:57,621 --> 00:21:59,156
WOW.

604
00:21:59,156 --> 00:22:00,024
WHOO!

605
00:22:00,024 --> 00:22:02,526
SO YOU GUYS LEARNED
ALL ABOUT POSING LIKE ANIMALS.

606
00:22:02,526 --> 00:22:04,962
SO, OF COURSE, WE'RE GONNA DO
A PHOTO SHOOT TODAY,

607
00:22:04,962 --> 00:22:07,998
BUT YOU GUYS ARE GOING TO BE
THE ANIMALS.

608
00:22:07,998 --> 00:22:09,199
SO I PICKED AN ANIMAL

609
00:22:09,199 --> 00:22:11,602
THAT I THINK REPRESENTS EACH
AND ALL OF YOU.

610
00:22:11,602 --> 00:22:12,903
I'M GONNA START WITH YOU,
THEN, KAHLEN.

611
00:22:12,903 --> 00:22:15,339
YOU ARE ACTUALLY GOING TO BE
A SPRINGBOK.

612
00:22:15,339 --> 00:22:18,642
SPRINGBOK IS
SOUTH AFRICA'S NATIONAL ANIMAL.

613
00:22:18,642 --> 00:22:20,310
CHRISTINA, YOU'RE GONNA BE
AN OSTRICH.

614
00:22:20,310 --> 00:22:21,412
OH, WOW.

615
00:22:21,412 --> 00:22:23,881
BRITTANY, YOU ARE
SO TALL AND LONG,

616
00:22:23,881 --> 00:22:24,615
YOU'RE GONNA BE...

617
00:22:24,615 --> 00:22:25,182
A GIRAFFE!

618
00:22:25,182 --> 00:22:25,983
A GIRAFFE.

619
00:22:25,983 --> 00:22:27,451
MICHELLE, WE'RE GONNA
MAKE YOU A ZEBRA.

620
00:22:27,451 --> 00:22:28,619
OH, THERE WE GO!

621
00:22:28,619 --> 00:22:30,154
I THINK THAT'S APPROPRIATE

622
00:22:30,154 --> 00:22:31,789
BECAUSE ZEBRAS
ARE KIND OF SKITTISH

623
00:22:31,789 --> 00:22:32,656
AND KIND OF AFRAID.

624
00:22:32,656 --> 00:22:34,758
NAIMA, SILENT PREDATOR...

625
00:22:34,758 --> 00:22:35,459
OH, NO.

626
00:22:35,459 --> 00:22:36,326
CHEETAH.

627
00:22:36,326 --> 00:22:37,661
A CHEETAH.

628
00:22:37,661 --> 00:22:38,262
ALL RIGHT?

629
00:22:38,262 --> 00:22:38,962
OKAY.

630
00:22:38,962 --> 00:22:40,964
KEENYAH, YOU GET TO BE
THE ELEPHANT.

631
00:22:40,964 --> 00:22:41,865
I DON'T KNOW HOW--

632
00:22:41,865 --> 00:22:43,500
(laughter)

633
00:22:43,500 --> 00:22:46,103
ONE WEEK IT'S GLUTTONY,
THE NEXT WEEK IT'S AN ELEPHANT.

634
00:22:46,103 --> 00:22:47,538
RIGHT.

635
00:22:47,538 --> 00:22:49,940
EVERYBODY ELSE HAS
THESE SEXY LITTLE ANIMALS,

636
00:22:49,940 --> 00:22:52,176
AND I GET TO BE
THE BIG, FAT ELEPHANT.

637
00:22:52,176 --> 00:22:53,343
WHY DO I KEEP
GETTING STUCK WITH

638
00:22:53,343 --> 00:22:55,279
THESE FAT, LIKE, CHARACTERS?

639
00:22:55,279 --> 00:22:56,280
WHAT IS GOING ON?

640
00:22:58,082 --> 00:22:59,349
OH, IS THAT A GATOR?

641
00:22:59,349 --> 00:22:59,950
WHERE?

642
00:22:59,950 --> 00:23:01,018
RIGHT THERE.

643
00:23:01,018 --> 00:23:02,186
WOW.

644
00:23:02,186 --> 00:23:02,753
OH, REALLY?

645
00:23:02,753 --> 00:23:04,288
OH, MY GOD.

646
00:23:04,288 --> 00:23:05,422
ALL RIGHT,
SO TODAY'S SHOOT

647
00:23:05,422 --> 00:23:08,258
IS FOR LUBRIDERM
ULTRA-MOISTURIZING LOTION

648
00:23:08,258 --> 00:23:09,693
WITH PREMIUM OAT EXTRACTS,

649
00:23:09,693 --> 00:23:12,029
AND, OF COURSE, THAT'S WHY
WE'VE GOT THE CROCODILE.

650
00:23:12,029 --> 00:23:13,497
SO I WANT TO INTRODUCE YOU
TO YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER.

651
00:23:13,497 --> 00:23:14,198
HER NAME IS GERDA.

652
00:23:14,198 --> 00:23:15,766
GERDA, YOU WANNA COME OUT
AND MEET THE GIRLS?

653
00:23:15,766 --> 00:23:16,366
HI, GIRLS.

654
00:23:16,366 --> 00:23:17,367
HI.

655
00:23:17,367 --> 00:23:18,535
THEY'RE BEAUTIFUL, RIGHT?

656
00:23:18,535 --> 00:23:19,303
WONDERFUL.

657
00:23:19,303 --> 00:23:21,038
WE GOTTA GET YOU GUYS
BACK TO HAIR AND MAKEUP,

658
00:23:21,038 --> 00:23:22,272
TURN YOU INTO SOME ANIMALS.

659
00:23:22,272 --> 00:23:23,474
YOU'RE A SEXY ZEBRA.

660
00:23:27,644 --> 00:23:28,679
THINK TRUNK.

661
00:23:28,679 --> 00:23:29,246
TRUNK?

662
00:23:29,246 --> 00:23:30,080
TRUNK.

663
00:23:31,982 --> 00:23:33,484
HAVE YOU BEEN THINKING
ABOUT OSTRICHES

664
00:23:33,484 --> 00:23:34,384
WHILE YOU'VE BEEN
IN HAIR AND MAKEUP?

665
00:23:34,384 --> 00:23:34,852
YES.

666
00:23:34,852 --> 00:23:36,753
NOW AND YOU'RE WORKING
WITH MARY OBVIOUSLY.

667
00:23:36,753 --> 00:23:37,287
YES.

668
00:23:37,287 --> 00:23:39,189
SO I DON'T WANT TO
SEE NERVES.

669
00:23:39,189 --> 00:23:39,690
'CAUSE, YOU KNOW,

670
00:23:39,690 --> 00:23:41,058
THE COMPETITION'S GETTING
SO TIGHT...

671
00:23:41,058 --> 00:23:41,625
IT IS.

672
00:23:41,625 --> 00:23:42,459
WHO'S GONNA BE ELIMINATED

673
00:23:42,459 --> 00:23:45,295
IS REALLY DEPENDENT
ON THIS PHOTO SHOOT, OKAY?

674
00:23:45,295 --> 00:23:46,029
GOT IT.

675
00:23:47,764 --> 00:23:48,999
CABARET LIKE.

676
00:23:48,999 --> 00:23:49,933
GOOD, YES.

677
00:23:49,933 --> 00:23:51,235
PRETTY.
OH, I LOVE THAT.

678
00:23:51,235 --> 00:23:53,036
BEAUTIFUL, ELEGANT, YES.

679
00:23:53,036 --> 00:23:53,804
IF WE COULD JUST HAVE

680
00:23:53,804 --> 00:23:55,939
A LITTLE MORE WARMTH
IN THE FACE?

681
00:23:55,939 --> 00:23:57,307
THINK OF
SOMETHING PLEASANT,

682
00:23:57,307 --> 00:23:59,610
LIKE LOLLIPOPS
IN THE AFTERNOON.

683
00:23:59,610 --> 00:24:00,811
(laughs)

684
00:24:00,811 --> 00:24:01,745
ANYTHING?

685
00:24:01,745 --> 00:24:03,313
WHAT ABOUT YOUR HEAD
IN MARY'S MOUTH?

686
00:24:03,313 --> 00:24:04,348
YES!

687
00:24:04,348 --> 00:24:06,984
YES! OH, MY GOD. YES!

688
00:24:06,984 --> 00:24:10,320
FOR THE FIRST TIME, WE GOT
REAL EMOTION OUT OF HER.

689
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:13,090
I THINK THIS IS CHRISTINA'S
BEST SHOOT SO FAR.

690
00:24:13,090 --> 00:24:14,458
YEAH, THERE YOU GO.
YES!

691
00:24:14,458 --> 00:24:16,360
OH, MY GOD.
ANOTHER SMILE.

692
00:24:16,360 --> 00:24:17,294
ALL RIGHT, MY DEAR.

693
00:24:17,294 --> 00:24:18,629
GO AHEAD AND WORK IT.

694
00:24:18,629 --> 00:24:21,665
I WALKED IN THE SHOOT
FEELING AMAZING.

695
00:24:21,665 --> 00:24:23,433
I WAS READY TO
HOP UP THERE ON THAT ROCK

696
00:24:23,433 --> 00:24:26,236
WITH THE ALLIGATOR
AND JUST DO MY THING.

697
00:24:26,236 --> 00:24:27,304
WHOA. WHOA. WHOA.

698
00:24:29,006 --> 00:24:31,041
THAT'S LOOKING
A BIT LIKE A CRANE

699
00:24:31,041 --> 00:24:32,242
AND LESS LIKE A ZEBRA.

700
00:24:32,242 --> 00:24:35,012
THINK MORE GRACEFUL
'CAUSE YOU DO THIS A LOT.

701
00:24:35,012 --> 00:24:35,812
BETTER.

702
00:24:35,812 --> 00:24:37,147
RELAX.

703
00:24:37,147 --> 00:24:38,849
DON'T FORGET YOUR NECK,
MICHELLE.

704
00:24:38,849 --> 00:24:42,019
EVERY SHOOT TO DATE, I HAVE
TOLD MICHELLE TO DROP HER CHIN

705
00:24:42,019 --> 00:24:44,922
AND TRUST THE EYE LINE
FROM HER EYE TO THE CAMERA.

706
00:24:44,922 --> 00:24:46,023
THAT LOOKS GREAT.

707
00:24:46,023 --> 00:24:47,357
IF YOU JUST HOLD THAT
AND WORK THAT,

708
00:24:47,357 --> 00:24:48,425
THAT'D BE PERFECT.

709
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:51,795
LOVELY. LOVE THAT.

710
00:24:51,795 --> 00:24:56,200
NAIMA--SHE POSES RIGHT DOWN
TO THE TIPPY TOES OF HER FEET.

711
00:24:56,200 --> 00:24:57,000
BEAUTIFUL.

712
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:57,768
A LITTLE SMIRK.

713
00:24:57,768 --> 00:24:59,703
YOU THINK OF EVERYTHING
AND YOU FORGET THE MOUTH.

714
00:24:59,703 --> 00:25:01,471
THAT'S ONE THING.

715
00:25:01,471 --> 00:25:03,540
SHE'S THE SILENT KILLER.

716
00:25:03,540 --> 00:25:05,042
HOW COME YOU JUST
GET TO CRAWL AROUND

717
00:25:05,042 --> 00:25:06,577
AND I GOTTA WORK
WITH A CANE?

718
00:25:06,577 --> 00:25:08,946
I DIDN'T QUITE LIKE MY LOOK,

719
00:25:08,946 --> 00:25:11,582
BUT I REALLY WANT
THIS PHOTO SHOOT

720
00:25:11,582 --> 00:25:14,017
TO PULL THROUGH AND BRING ME
ANOTHER GREAT PICTURE.

721
00:25:14,017 --> 00:25:15,118
IT COULD BE WORSE.

722
00:25:15,118 --> 00:25:16,420
YOU COULD BE AN ELEPHANT.

723
00:25:18,956 --> 00:25:19,756
I'M FREAKING OUT.

724
00:25:19,756 --> 00:25:20,924
LIKE,
"WHAT AM I GONNA DO?"

725
00:25:20,924 --> 00:25:22,659
I DON'T KNOW HOW TO BE
A SEXY ELEPHANT.

726
00:25:22,659 --> 00:25:26,930
THE STOMACH IS EXPOSED
TO THE HIGHEST EXTENT,

727
00:25:26,930 --> 00:25:29,833
AND IT'S BLOATED, AND IT
DOESN'T LOOK GOOD AT ALL.

728
00:25:29,833 --> 00:25:32,369
I HAVE TO JUST TRY
TO SUCK IT IN AND WORK IT.

729
00:25:34,905 --> 00:25:37,674
THINK OF YOUR ARM AS
AN EXTENSION OF YOUR NOSE.

730
00:25:37,674 --> 00:25:39,610
IT'S GOT TO BE IN YOUR MIND,
THEN WE'LL BELIEVE IT.

731
00:25:41,878 --> 00:25:42,879
THINK OF IT, KEENYAH.

732
00:25:42,879 --> 00:25:44,014
RIGHT NOW
YOU'RE JUST HOLDING IT.

733
00:25:44,014 --> 00:25:45,549
NOW YOU'RE HOLDING
THAT BOTTLE AGAIN.

734
00:25:45,549 --> 00:25:46,350
IT'S NOT A TRUNK.

735
00:25:46,350 --> 00:25:47,417
THAT'S MY TENTH TIME.

736
00:25:47,417 --> 00:25:49,019
KEENYAH--SHE JUST
KIND OF POSES

737
00:25:49,019 --> 00:25:50,721
AND JUST HOPES
THAT IT WORKS.

738
00:25:50,721 --> 00:25:53,323
THAT'S NOT
THE BEST WAY TO MODEL.

739
00:25:53,323 --> 00:25:58,161
♪♪♪

740
00:25:58,161 --> 00:25:59,563
IT DOESN'T HAVE TO GET
TOO STIFF.

741
00:25:59,563 --> 00:26:02,566
YOU'RE A CUDDLY,
TALL GIRAFFE.

742
00:26:02,566 --> 00:26:04,434
BRITTANY--I KNOW SHE HAD
A LOT TO DEAL WITH,

743
00:26:04,434 --> 00:26:06,970
BUT SHE
WASN'T AS AWARE OF HER FACE.

744
00:26:06,970 --> 00:26:08,905
YOU'RE GETTING
A LITTLE STILTED.

745
00:26:08,905 --> 00:26:10,907
A LITTLE SMILE, YES.

746
00:26:10,907 --> 00:26:14,611
IN MIDDLE SCHOOL,
I WAS ALWAYS CALLED GIRAFFE.

747
00:26:14,611 --> 00:26:15,646
IT HURT MY FEELINGS.

748
00:26:15,646 --> 00:26:18,782
SO IT'S JUST KINDA FUN NOW
TO BE A SEXY GIRAFFE

749
00:26:18,782 --> 00:26:19,983
AND BE LIKE, "HA!"

750
00:26:19,983 --> 00:26:20,817
OOH, YES.

751
00:26:20,817 --> 00:26:22,886
THAT'S NICE. YES.

752
00:26:22,886 --> 00:26:24,121
THAT'S GREAT.

753
00:26:26,623 --> 00:26:27,924
KAHLEN,
IT'S COMING FOR YOU.

754
00:26:29,526 --> 00:26:31,328
OUR SPRINGBOK.

755
00:26:31,328 --> 00:26:33,830
IT'S NOT A DEER,
IT'S A SPRINGBOK.

756
00:26:33,830 --> 00:26:36,266
YES. YES.

757
00:26:36,266 --> 00:26:37,701
THAT'S GREAT, KAHLEN.

758
00:26:37,701 --> 00:26:39,002
WHAT ARE YOU DOING
WITH THE HAND IN THE MIDDLE?

759
00:26:39,002 --> 00:26:39,970
I'M CURIOUS.

760
00:26:39,970 --> 00:26:42,339
LIKE, I JUST DON'T GET
WHAT THIS IS.

761
00:26:42,339 --> 00:26:44,174
WHOO!

762
00:26:44,174 --> 00:26:45,475
THAT--THAT'S MUCH BETTER.

763
00:26:45,475 --> 00:26:46,443
YES, NICE.

764
00:26:46,443 --> 00:26:49,046
OOH, I ACTUALLY LOVE THAT.
NICE, YES!

765
00:26:49,046 --> 00:26:53,150
KAHLEN DID THE BEST JOB
OF TAKING ON HER ANIMAL.

766
00:26:59,022 --> 00:27:00,157
I TOLD HER,
IF ANYTHING HAPPENS,

767
00:27:00,157 --> 00:27:01,591
LET GO OF
THELUBRIDERM AND GO,

768
00:27:01,591 --> 00:27:04,661
AND SHE JUST SPLIT OUTTA THERE
LIKE A SPRINGBOK WOULD.

769
00:27:04,661 --> 00:27:06,563
THEY KINDA
PRANCE AND BOUNCE.

770
00:27:06,563 --> 00:27:07,798
(laughs)

771
00:27:07,798 --> 00:27:08,899
JAWS.

772
00:27:08,899 --> 00:27:13,236
♪♪♪

773
00:27:13,236 --> 00:27:15,472
IT'S OUR FIRST NIGHT OUT
TO DINNER IN SOUTH AFRICA,

774
00:27:15,472 --> 00:27:17,941
AND WE WERE GOING TO
A RESTAURANT CALLED FIVE FLIES.

775
00:27:17,941 --> 00:27:19,543
IT'S BEEN A LONG DAY
OUT IN THE SUN.

776
00:27:19,543 --> 00:27:20,744
WE'RE HAPPY TO EAT.

777
00:27:22,179 --> 00:27:23,013
I WENT ON THE SET,

778
00:27:23,013 --> 00:27:24,815
AND THEN JAY HANDS ME
THE LUBRIDERM BOTTLE,

779
00:27:24,815 --> 00:27:26,350
AND I WENT LIKE THIS...

780
00:27:26,350 --> 00:27:27,818
HONEST TO GOD.

781
00:27:27,818 --> 00:27:29,419
I THOUGHT HE WAS
JUST HANDING ME LOTION.

782
00:27:29,419 --> 00:27:29,853
AND HE WAS LIKE,

783
00:27:29,853 --> 00:27:31,488
"NO, THIS IS WHAT
YOU'RE MODELING, HONEY."

784
00:27:31,488 --> 00:27:32,422
I'M LIKE...

785
00:27:32,422 --> 00:27:34,257
(laughter)

786
00:27:38,729 --> 00:27:40,530
MICHELLE,
DO YOU FEEL ALIENATED?

787
00:27:45,802 --> 00:27:48,305
NAIMA--I'M SURPRISED
WHEN SHE SAYS THAT.

788
00:27:48,305 --> 00:27:49,539
I MEAN, IT WAS KINDA
OUTTA THE BLUE.

789
00:27:49,539 --> 00:27:51,174
I DON'T WANT TO
SAY ANYTHING,

790
00:27:51,174 --> 00:27:53,310
BECAUSE
IT'S NOT PURELY THEM.

791
00:27:53,310 --> 00:27:54,811
IT'S MOSTLY ME.

792
00:27:54,811 --> 00:27:57,080
I MEAN, I HAVE HAD
A HARD TIME WITH IT,

793
00:27:57,080 --> 00:27:59,583
BUT, I MEAN, I'M TRYING TO GET
MORE IN WITH THE GROUP.

794
00:27:59,583 --> 00:28:01,785
BUT YOU'VE BEEN
AROUND US SO LONG, MICHELLE.

795
00:28:01,785 --> 00:28:04,421
YOU SHOULDN'T FEEL
THE NEED TO BE DISTANT.

796
00:28:04,421 --> 00:28:07,791
I'M JUST KIND OF
OVER MICHELLE AT THIS POINT.

797
00:28:07,791 --> 00:28:09,793
I FEEL, IF YOU'RE NOT GONNA
GET IN WITH US

798
00:28:09,793 --> 00:28:11,128
SINCE WE'VE BEEN HERE,

799
00:28:11,128 --> 00:28:13,130
THAT I JUST DON'T FEEL LIKE
IT'S GONNA HAPPEN NOW.

800
00:28:13,130 --> 00:28:14,297
WAITING FOR MAIL?

801
00:28:14,297 --> 00:28:17,134
OH, THANK YOU SO MUCH.

802
00:28:17,134 --> 00:28:19,035
"YOU'VE BEEN OUT
WHERE THE LIONS ROAM.

803
00:28:19,035 --> 00:28:21,271
"NOW HEAD OUT
TO YOUR SEASIDE HOME.

804
00:28:21,271 --> 00:28:22,873
TYRA."

805
00:28:22,873 --> 00:28:24,641
PSYCH. IT SAYS...

806
00:28:24,641 --> 00:28:27,177
NO, IT REALLY SAYS
"YOUR SEASIDE HOME."

807
00:28:27,177 --> 00:28:31,581
♪♪♪

808
00:28:31,581 --> 00:28:32,783
ROOM READY?

809
00:28:32,783 --> 00:28:34,284
WHOO-HOO!

810
00:28:34,284 --> 00:28:35,519
WHOO!

811
00:28:35,519 --> 00:28:37,554
VERY, VERY GROOVY, BABY.

812
00:28:37,554 --> 00:28:39,055
OUR HOTEL SUITE IS
REALLY, REALLY NICE.

813
00:28:39,055 --> 00:28:40,991
WE ARE ON THE WATER,
AND TO ME,

814
00:28:40,991 --> 00:28:42,259
THE OCEAN IS SO CALMING,

815
00:28:42,259 --> 00:28:44,227
AND ESPECIALLY IN A SITUATION
WHERE WE'RE SO STRESSED.

816
00:28:44,227 --> 00:28:47,864
THIS IS PHAT,
AND THAT MEANS WITH A "P-H."

817
00:28:47,864 --> 00:28:50,100
I DON'T NEED YOU
TO FINGER ALL OF THE CANDY.

818
00:28:50,100 --> 00:28:51,768
TYRA MAIL!

819
00:28:51,768 --> 00:28:53,703
"TOMORROW YOU WILL MEET
WITH THE JUDGES.

820
00:28:53,703 --> 00:28:55,372
"ONLY FIVE OF YOU
WILL CONTINUE

821
00:28:55,372 --> 00:28:58,809
"IN THE HOPES OF BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

822
00:28:58,809 --> 00:29:00,944
ONE OF YOU
WILL BE ELIMINATED."

823
00:29:02,412 --> 00:29:04,014
I FEEL LIKE MY STANDING
IN THE COMPETITION

824
00:29:04,014 --> 00:29:06,049
IS PRETTY STRONG,
BUT THEN AGAIN,

825
00:29:06,049 --> 00:29:08,285
I COULD BE WRONG BECAUSE
EVERY TIME I GO TO PANEL,

826
00:29:08,285 --> 00:29:10,020
IT'S ANOTHER PROBLEM
THAT THEY PRESENT.

827
00:29:10,020 --> 00:29:11,688
I'M STILL PART ELEPHANT.

828
00:29:11,688 --> 00:29:14,858
I HAVE SOME NERVES
WORKING UP INSIDE OF ME.

829
00:29:14,858 --> 00:29:16,460
I WOULD BE INSANE
IF I DIDN'T.

830
00:29:16,460 --> 00:29:19,896
I AM PRAYING
THAT MY PHOTO IS GOOD.

831
00:29:25,602 --> 00:29:34,945
♪♪♪

832
00:29:34,945 --> 00:29:36,379
WELCOME TO YOUR VERY FIRST

833
00:29:36,379 --> 00:29:38,915
SOUTH AFRICAN JUDGING
EXPERIENCE.

834
00:29:38,915 --> 00:29:41,384
NOW IT'S TIME TO MAKE
OUR NINTH CUT,

835
00:29:41,384 --> 00:29:43,253
WHICH WILL BRING US
ONE STEP CLOSER

836
00:29:43,253 --> 00:29:44,254
TOWARDS DETERMINING

837
00:29:44,254 --> 00:29:46,990
WHO WILL BECOME
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

838
00:29:46,990 --> 00:29:49,159
NOW YOU GUYS KNOW
ABOUT THE FABULOUS PRIZES--

839
00:29:49,159 --> 00:29:51,294
A CONTRACT FROM TOP
INTERNATIONAL

840
00:29:51,294 --> 00:29:53,463
MODEL MANAGEMENT
COMPANY, FORD MODELS,

841
00:29:53,463 --> 00:29:55,866
A PHOTO SPREAD
IN "ELLE" MAGAZINE,

842
00:29:55,866 --> 00:29:57,133
WHICH WILL BE SHOT BY

843
00:29:57,133 --> 00:29:59,269
WORLD-RENOWNED PHOTOGRAPHER
GILLES BENSIMONE,

844
00:29:59,269 --> 00:30:03,540
AND A $100,000 CONTRACT
WITH COVER GIRL COSMETICS.

845
00:30:03,540 --> 00:30:05,342
WE HAVE OUR AMAZING JUDGES,

846
00:30:05,342 --> 00:30:07,110
THE FIRST BEING
MISS JANICE DICKINSON,

847
00:30:07,110 --> 00:30:08,945
ONE OF THE WORLD'S FIRST
SUPERMODELS,

848
00:30:08,945 --> 00:30:11,414
NIGEL BARKER,
NOTED FASHION PHOTOGRAPHER,

849
00:30:11,414 --> 00:30:14,451
NOLE MARIN, PROMINENT
FASHION EDITOR AND STYLIST,

850
00:30:14,451 --> 00:30:15,752
AND GERDA,

851
00:30:15,752 --> 00:30:17,454
WHO WAS YOUR PHOTOGRAPHER
THIS WEEK

852
00:30:17,454 --> 00:30:18,688
FOR YOUR PHOTO SHOOT.

853
00:30:18,688 --> 00:30:20,357
THIS WEEK YOU LEARNED
ALL ABOUT POSING,

854
00:30:20,357 --> 00:30:22,592
SO TODAY WE'RE GONNA TEST YOU
ON YOUR POSING SKILLS.

855
00:30:22,592 --> 00:30:24,561
THE JUDGES HAVE
FIVE DIFFERENT OBJECTS

856
00:30:24,561 --> 00:30:26,429
HIDDEN
UNDERNEATH THIS TABLE.

857
00:30:26,429 --> 00:30:28,331
THE JUDGES ARE GONNA
HAND YOU A OBJECT

858
00:30:28,331 --> 00:30:31,434
AND GIVE YOU A WORD
THAT YOU HAVE TO ACT OUT.

859
00:30:31,434 --> 00:30:33,336
YOU HAVE ONE POSE
PER OBJECT.

860
00:30:33,336 --> 00:30:34,471
YOU HAVE TO STRIKE IT FAST,

861
00:30:34,471 --> 00:30:36,072
AND YOU HAVE TO
STRIKE IT STRONG.

862
00:30:36,072 --> 00:30:37,741
WORK IT, GIRLFRIEND.

863
00:30:37,741 --> 00:30:38,542
WORK IT.

864
00:30:38,542 --> 00:30:40,844
YOUR EMOTION,
MY DEAR--ANGER.

865
00:30:40,844 --> 00:30:41,745
JUST ANY TIME?

866
00:30:41,745 --> 00:30:42,979
NO, WAIT AN HOUR.

867
00:30:42,979 --> 00:30:50,520
♪♪♪

868
00:30:52,022 --> 00:30:54,591
(trumpet plays
"Wah-Wah" sound)

869
00:30:54,591 --> 00:30:56,626
♪♪♪

870
00:30:56,626 --> 00:30:58,962
AND THIS NEXT IS FEAR.

871
00:30:58,962 --> 00:31:04,367
(sneaky music playing)

872
00:31:08,538 --> 00:31:09,606
ALOOF.

873
00:31:10,874 --> 00:31:12,042
WHAT IS ALOOF?

874
00:31:12,042 --> 00:31:13,510
COULD I HAVE A HINT?

875
00:31:13,510 --> 00:31:14,945
ALOOF.

876
00:31:14,945 --> 00:31:15,745
ALOOF?

877
00:31:15,745 --> 00:31:16,646
ALOOF.

878
00:31:16,646 --> 00:31:17,414
ALOOF.

879
00:31:17,414 --> 00:31:18,114
ALOOF.

880
00:31:18,114 --> 00:31:19,416
I CAN'T ASK WHAT ALOOF IS?

881
00:31:19,416 --> 00:31:20,383
NO.

882
00:31:24,955 --> 00:31:26,690
THERE YOU GO.
PASSION.

883
00:31:26,690 --> 00:31:34,230
(funk music playing)

884
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:38,501
(music slows and stops)

885
00:31:38,501 --> 00:31:39,936
HERE YOU GO, MICHELLE.

886
00:31:39,936 --> 00:31:40,971
HAPPINESS.

887
00:31:40,971 --> 00:31:49,446
(ragtime music playing)

888
00:31:49,446 --> 00:31:51,081
(laughter)

889
00:31:51,081 --> 00:31:53,316
NOW WE'RE GONNA DO
YOUR INDIVIDUAL EVALUATIONS.

890
00:31:53,316 --> 00:31:54,684
FIRST IS MICHELLE.

891
00:31:54,684 --> 00:31:57,153
YOUR BEST POSE WAS FEAR.

892
00:31:57,153 --> 00:31:58,755
YOU LOOKED QUITE SCARED
THE WHOLE TIME.

893
00:31:58,755 --> 00:32:01,725
YOU HAD A PHOTO SHOOT WHERE
YOU HAD TO EVOKE AN ANIMAL--

894
00:32:01,725 --> 00:32:03,827
THE LOOK, THE TOUCH,
THE FEEL, THE SMELL--

895
00:32:03,827 --> 00:32:04,828
NOT THE SMELL.

896
00:32:04,828 --> 00:32:06,997
AND HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

897
00:32:06,997 --> 00:32:07,731
WOW.

898
00:32:07,731 --> 00:32:08,965
YOU WERE SCARED
IN FRONT OF US,

899
00:32:08,965 --> 00:32:09,833
GIVING US THE EMOTIONS,

900
00:32:09,833 --> 00:32:12,369
YET SOMEHOW YOU MANAGED
TO PULL OFF SORT OF PASSION

901
00:32:12,369 --> 00:32:14,237
AND LUST WITH AN ALLIGATOR
BETWEEN YOUR LEGS.

902
00:32:14,237 --> 00:32:14,904
I LIKE THIS SHOT.

903
00:32:14,904 --> 00:32:16,506
I DON'T LOVE IT,
BUT I REALLY LIKE IT.

904
00:32:16,506 --> 00:32:18,642
IT'S NOT GOOD ENOUGH!

905
00:32:18,642 --> 00:32:20,210
YOU'RE NOT PORTRAYING
AN ANIMAL.

906
00:32:20,210 --> 00:32:22,312
YOU WERE BORN WITH
BEAUTIFUL LOOKS,

907
00:32:22,312 --> 00:32:24,914
BUT IT'S A HELL OF A LOT MORE
THAN THAT, HONEY.

908
00:32:24,914 --> 00:32:25,615
NAIMA.

909
00:32:25,615 --> 00:32:27,751
WHEN YOU WERE POSING,
YOU WERE ALMOST THERE,

910
00:32:27,751 --> 00:32:30,053
LIKE OUT OF TEN YOU WERE LIKE
EIGHT AND A HALF, NINE.

911
00:32:30,053 --> 00:32:31,087
PASSION.

912
00:32:31,087 --> 00:32:32,389
I DIDN'T FIND IT.

913
00:32:32,389 --> 00:32:33,623
CAN YOU DO PASSION?

914
00:32:33,623 --> 00:32:35,692
OOH.

915
00:32:35,692 --> 00:32:37,894
BUT SEE THE FACE--
THE FACE GOT UGLY.

916
00:32:37,894 --> 00:32:38,795
YOU DID ELVIS.

917
00:32:38,795 --> 00:32:40,664
HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

918
00:32:40,664 --> 00:32:41,931
SHE'S A CHEETAH.

919
00:32:41,931 --> 00:32:42,832
- AMAZING.
- WELL DONE.

920
00:32:42,832 --> 00:32:44,601
I WOULD LOVE TO HAVE SEEN
YOUR RIGHT LEG

921
00:32:44,601 --> 00:32:46,036
NOT LOOK LIKE AN AMPUTEE.

922
00:32:46,036 --> 00:32:47,070
I THINK THE LEG IS FINE.

923
00:32:47,070 --> 00:32:48,972
UNFORTUNATELY,
I AGREE WITH JANICE.

924
00:32:48,972 --> 00:32:50,674
I THINK THE BODY COULD HAVE
MORE ELEGANCE.

925
00:32:50,674 --> 00:32:51,841
COME ON, YOU GUYS,
WHAT DO YOU SEE?

926
00:32:51,841 --> 00:32:54,010
SHE'S BEING AN ANIMAL
AND A MODEL AT THE SAME TIME.

927
00:32:54,010 --> 00:32:55,178
SHE WAS THE ONE PERSON

928
00:32:55,178 --> 00:32:57,380
THAT USED HER LIMBS
LIKE THE ANIMAL,

929
00:32:57,380 --> 00:32:59,049
AND THAT'S BRILLIANT.

930
00:32:59,049 --> 00:32:59,649
KEENYAH.

931
00:32:59,649 --> 00:33:01,151
YOU HAVE TO MODEL
WITH YOUR WHOLE BODY.

932
00:33:01,151 --> 00:33:02,085
THE OTHER GIRLS
GOT ON THE GROUND,

933
00:33:02,085 --> 00:33:04,220
GOT UP, MOVED AROUND,
HELD THINGS IN THE AIR.

934
00:33:04,220 --> 00:33:05,588
YOU WERE LIKE THIS
THE WHOLE TIME.

935
00:33:05,588 --> 00:33:08,458
ALOOF AND PASSION WERE
EXACTLY THE SAME THING.

936
00:33:08,458 --> 00:33:10,960
IT WAS LIKE GROUNDHOG'S DAY.

937
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:11,661
WOW.

938
00:33:11,661 --> 00:33:13,229
- WOW, WHAT?
- BEAUTIFUL FACE.

939
00:33:13,229 --> 00:33:15,999
THIS IS A BEAUTIFUL SHOT,
AND IT HAS AN ELEGANCE

940
00:33:15,999 --> 00:33:18,201
THAT ELEPHANTS HAVE
DESPITE THEIR HEAVINESS.

941
00:33:18,201 --> 00:33:19,703
THIS PHOTO IS
REALLY BEAUTIFUL, KEENYAH,

942
00:33:19,703 --> 00:33:21,471
BUT I HATE TO SAY IT--
THEY HAD TO DO

943
00:33:21,471 --> 00:33:23,907
A LOT OF BODY WORK ON YOU
IN RETOUCHING.

944
00:33:23,907 --> 00:33:25,975
AT HOME, PRETTY MUCH I TRY
TO, YOU KNOW, EAT RIGHT,

945
00:33:25,975 --> 00:33:27,610
AND WE COME HERE,
MY METABOLISM,

946
00:33:27,610 --> 00:33:28,511
EVERYTHING IS THROWN OFF.

947
00:33:28,511 --> 00:33:29,179
STOP!

948
00:33:29,179 --> 00:33:30,680
IF YOU'RE SPORTING A GUT,

949
00:33:30,680 --> 00:33:33,783
THEN YOU TURN TO THE SIDE
AND DISGUISE IT.

950
00:33:33,783 --> 00:33:36,252
KEENYAH, IN THE REAL WORLD,
YOU'RE A THIN GIRL,

951
00:33:36,252 --> 00:33:38,455
BUT THE FASHION INDUSTRY
IS SO EXTREME,

952
00:33:38,455 --> 00:33:39,989
AND I WOULD LOVE TO CHANGE
THE RULES,

953
00:33:39,989 --> 00:33:41,157
BUT UNTIL THAT HAPPENS,

954
00:33:41,157 --> 00:33:42,525
I THINK IT'S ALL
ABOUT CHOICES, KEENYAH.

955
00:33:42,525 --> 00:33:44,394
YOU CAN GET A BURGER
AND TAKE THE BREAD OFF.

956
00:33:44,394 --> 00:33:45,695
I MAKE IT WORK
WHEN I HAVE TO.

957
00:33:45,695 --> 00:33:46,496
THANK YOU.

958
00:33:46,496 --> 00:33:47,997
NOW I CAN EAT
WHATEVER THE HELL I WANT.

959
00:33:47,997 --> 00:33:50,233
THEY'LL RETOUCH IT, YOU KNOW,
BECAUSE I PAID MY DUES.

960
00:33:50,233 --> 00:33:51,735
I SAW YOU EATING
THOSE BURGERS.

961
00:33:51,735 --> 00:33:52,902
I DO. I EAT.

962
00:33:52,902 --> 00:33:54,437
SHE EATS THOSE RIBS.

963
00:33:54,437 --> 00:33:55,271
YOU'RE NEW.

964
00:33:55,271 --> 00:33:57,140
BE HONEST WITH YOURSELF
AND DON'T POINT THE FINGER,

965
00:33:57,140 --> 00:33:58,875
BECAUSE NOBODY WILL
RETOUCH A PICTURE

966
00:33:58,875 --> 00:34:01,177
AS MUCH
AS WE DID THIS PICTURE.

967
00:34:01,177 --> 00:34:03,379
CHRISTINA, I THOUGHT
YOUR HAPPINESS LOOKED CRAZY,

968
00:34:03,379 --> 00:34:05,548
LIKE, "HEH-HEH-HEH!
I'M GONNA GETCHA!"

969
00:34:05,548 --> 00:34:07,083
YOU KNOW?
YOU LOOKED INSANE.

970
00:34:07,083 --> 00:34:08,818
AND YOUR PASSION,
IT WAS LIKE,

971
00:34:08,818 --> 00:34:10,153
WHO'S TURNING YOU ON, MAN?

972
00:34:10,153 --> 00:34:12,655
'CAUSE HE DON'T KNOW
WHAT HE'S DOING.

973
00:34:12,655 --> 00:34:13,223
OH, MY GOODNESS.

974
00:34:13,223 --> 00:34:14,323
THIS WAS AN OSTRICH.

975
00:34:14,323 --> 00:34:16,792
THE LEGS ARE AMAZING,
BEAUTIFUL ARMS.

976
00:34:16,792 --> 00:34:18,727
THIS IS THE BEST PICTURE
YOU'VE EVER TAKEN.

977
00:34:18,727 --> 00:34:20,729
BUT YOUR WEAK SPOT
IS YOUR MOUTH.

978
00:34:20,729 --> 00:34:22,232
YOUR TOP LIP COULD BE
A LITTLE FULLER.

979
00:34:22,232 --> 00:34:23,066
THERE'S A TRICK.

980
00:34:23,066 --> 00:34:24,033
LET ME SHOW YOU.

981
00:34:24,033 --> 00:34:25,435
PEOPLE TELL YOU
YOU NEED SURGERY.

982
00:34:25,435 --> 00:34:26,602
YOU DON'T NEED SURGERY.

983
00:34:26,602 --> 00:34:29,839
UNDERNEATH YOUR TOP LIP,
STUFF THAT IN THERE.

984
00:34:29,839 --> 00:34:32,175
THIS IS WHAT
THE INDUSTRY IS ALL ABOUT--

985
00:34:32,175 --> 00:34:34,276
CHICKEN CUTLETS
FOR THE BREASTS.

986
00:34:34,276 --> 00:34:38,046
EVEN MEN STICK FAKE PENISES
DOWN THERE FOR UNDERWEAR JOBS.

987
00:34:38,046 --> 00:34:39,948
OH! LOOK AT IT.
LOOK AT IT.

988
00:34:39,948 --> 00:34:41,684
OH, MY GOD.
IT'S GORGEOUS.

989
00:34:41,684 --> 00:34:43,052
THIS IS YOUR TRICK.

990
00:34:43,052 --> 00:34:43,820
BRITTANY.

991
00:34:43,820 --> 00:34:45,988
BRITTANY WON THE POSING
CHALLENGE WITH MISS J.

992
00:34:45,988 --> 00:34:47,724
YOU MIGHT HAVE WON IT
IN LOS ANGELES,

993
00:34:47,724 --> 00:34:51,261
BUT THIS WAS JUST LIKE--
WHAT WAS THAT?

994
00:34:51,261 --> 00:34:53,263
WE'VE TOLD YOU
TIME AND TIME AGAIN

995
00:34:53,263 --> 00:34:55,031
JUST HOW GORGEOUS YOU ARE

996
00:34:55,031 --> 00:34:57,167
WHEN YOU ARE QUIET AND SIMPLE,
DOING JUST THAT.

997
00:34:57,167 --> 00:34:58,001
RIGHT NOW.

998
00:34:58,001 --> 00:34:59,468
IT'S ALLURING
AND NOT WHORING.

999
00:34:59,468 --> 00:35:00,770
THAT WAS THE KEY WORD THERE.

1000
00:35:01,805 --> 00:35:02,604
WOW, LOOK AT THAT.

1001
00:35:02,604 --> 00:35:03,573
AH, YOU ROCKED IT.

1002
00:35:03,573 --> 00:35:04,607
IT'S FANTASTIC.

1003
00:35:04,607 --> 00:35:05,675
BRITTANY,
DO YOU SEE YOUR FACE,

1004
00:35:05,675 --> 00:35:08,378
HOW PEACEFUL IT IS,
AND IT'S NATURALLY SEXY?

1005
00:35:08,378 --> 00:35:09,045
KAHLEN.

1006
00:35:09,045 --> 00:35:10,914
I MUST SAY, GIRL,
YOU ROCKED.

1007
00:35:10,914 --> 00:35:12,682
YOU WERE ABSOLUTELY AMAZING.

1008
00:35:12,682 --> 00:35:14,851
YOU COMMITTED SO MUCH
LIKE A PRO.

1009
00:35:14,851 --> 00:35:18,188
BUT THEN YOU GOT TO PASSION,
AND YOU KNOW WHAT TO DO,

1010
00:35:18,188 --> 00:35:19,656
BUT I FELT LIKE
YOU'RE HOLDING BACK

1011
00:35:19,656 --> 00:35:20,990
'CAUSE THAT'S TOO SEXY.

1012
00:35:20,990 --> 00:35:22,959
SO I WANNA SEE PASSION
RIGHT NOW.

1013
00:35:22,959 --> 00:35:24,861
NO, NOT POUTY--PASSION.

1014
00:35:24,861 --> 00:35:26,196
LET'S DO IT TOGETHER,
JANICE.

1015
00:35:26,196 --> 00:35:26,896
THIS IS PASSION.

1016
00:35:26,896 --> 00:35:29,332
IT'S SOMETHING THAT'S
SO EXAGGERATED, YOU GUYS.

1017
00:35:29,332 --> 00:35:31,501
YOU WANT TO SEE PASSION?

1018
00:35:31,501 --> 00:35:32,468
AAH!

1019
00:35:32,468 --> 00:35:34,604
(laughing)

1020
00:35:34,604 --> 00:35:35,972
I'LL SHOW YOU PASSION.

1021
00:35:38,274 --> 00:35:39,375
PERHAPS I CAN GET INVOLVED.

1022
00:35:39,375 --> 00:35:40,310
HELP!

1023
00:35:40,310 --> 00:35:42,111
JUST KIDDING. WAIT, WAIT!

1024
00:35:42,111 --> 00:35:42,946
PASSION!

1025
00:35:42,946 --> 00:35:45,582
(laughter)

1026
00:35:45,582 --> 00:35:46,015
CHILD.

1027
00:35:46,015 --> 00:35:47,183
IT'S JUST GIRLS HAVING FUN.

1028
00:35:47,183 --> 00:35:48,151
ALL RIGHT.

1029
00:35:49,385 --> 00:35:50,420
THAT'S PASSION.

1030
00:35:51,754 --> 00:35:52,889
YOU CAN'T HOLD BACK.

1031
00:35:53,957 --> 00:35:55,525
THAT WAS SCARY.

1032
00:35:55,525 --> 00:35:57,927
ALL RIGHT,
HERE IS YOUR BEST SHOT.

1033
00:35:57,927 --> 00:35:59,362
WILD KINGDOM, HERE WE COME.

1034
00:35:59,362 --> 00:36:00,597
YOU ARE A CHAMELEON.

1035
00:36:00,597 --> 00:36:01,631
YOU HAVE THE ABILITY

1036
00:36:01,631 --> 00:36:03,499
TO TURN INTO ANYTHING
AND EVERYTHING.

1037
00:36:03,499 --> 00:36:05,568
IT'S NOT SEXY,
BUT IT'S VERY COOL.

1038
00:36:05,568 --> 00:36:07,170
WERE YOU AFRAID
OF THE CROC?

1039
00:36:07,170 --> 00:36:08,504
SHE FELL ON TOP OF HIM.

1040
00:36:08,504 --> 00:36:09,505
YOU FELL ON THE CROC?

1041
00:36:09,505 --> 00:36:11,274
AND I RAN FASTER
THAN A SPRINGBOK.

1042
00:36:11,274 --> 00:36:13,176
GIRL, THAT'S A DRAG QUEEN
AFTER MY OWN HEART--

1043
00:36:13,176 --> 00:36:14,344
A GIRL IN
HIGH HEELS RUNNING.

1044
00:36:14,344 --> 00:36:15,378
(laughing)

1045
00:36:16,613 --> 00:36:17,347
NAIMA.

1046
00:36:17,347 --> 00:36:19,048
SHE LOOKS AMAZING
IN THIS PICTURE.

1047
00:36:19,048 --> 00:36:21,384
SHE WEARS THE SPOTS
OF A LEOPARD VERY WELL.

1048
00:36:21,384 --> 00:36:23,953
BUT I THINK
NAIMA HOLDS BACK A LOT.

1049
00:36:23,953 --> 00:36:24,520
BRITTANY.

1050
00:36:24,520 --> 00:36:26,923
BRITTANY HAS WHAT IT TAKES
TO BE A TOP MODEL.

1051
00:36:26,923 --> 00:36:28,825
SHE HAS THE PERSONALITY.

1052
00:36:28,825 --> 00:36:30,026
SHE'S AN EXAGGERATION.

1053
00:36:30,026 --> 00:36:31,794
SHE'S LIKE A WALKING
EXCLAMATION MARK,

1054
00:36:31,794 --> 00:36:33,630
AND IT'S NOT PRETTY.

1055
00:36:33,630 --> 00:36:34,464
MICHELLE.

1056
00:36:34,464 --> 00:36:36,532
MICHELLE--IN PERSON,
SHE'S JUST NOT THERE.

1057
00:36:36,532 --> 00:36:38,134
SHE'S WEAK.
SHE'S NERVOUS.

1058
00:36:38,134 --> 00:36:39,769
THERE IS A SILVER LINING
TO MICHELLE.

1059
00:36:39,769 --> 00:36:41,638
SHE CAN PULL OUT
A BEAUTIFUL PICTURE.

1060
00:36:41,638 --> 00:36:43,239
THAT'S THE SILVER LINING?

1061
00:36:43,239 --> 00:36:44,674
YES, THIS IS NOT
A BAD PICTURE.

1062
00:36:44,674 --> 00:36:45,675
THIS IS A GOOD PICTURE.

1063
00:36:45,675 --> 00:36:46,175
KAHLEN.

1064
00:36:46,175 --> 00:36:49,946
SHE REALLY GOT THIS DEER,
AND I KNOW THIS ANIMAL WELL.

1065
00:36:49,946 --> 00:36:51,147
HOW WELL DO YOU KNOW IT?

1066
00:36:51,147 --> 00:36:52,815
IT'S MY NATIONAL ANIMAL.

1067
00:36:52,815 --> 00:36:53,349
CHRISTINA.

1068
00:36:53,349 --> 00:36:54,217
SHE'S REALLY BROUGHT

1069
00:36:54,217 --> 00:36:55,818
HER BIRDLIKE FEATURES
TO A HEAD HERE.

1070
00:36:55,818 --> 00:36:57,020
THIS IS
THE PERFECT OSTRICH.

1071
00:36:57,020 --> 00:36:58,054
IN PERSON, CHRISTINA,

1072
00:36:58,054 --> 00:36:59,722
YOU WERE A LITTLE BIT
OF THAT ICE QUEEN AGAIN.

1073
00:36:59,722 --> 00:37:00,156
KEENYAH.

1074
00:37:00,156 --> 00:37:02,358
I THINK KEENYAH HAS HAD IT
TOO GOOD FOR TOO LONG.

1075
00:37:02,358 --> 00:37:04,093
KEENYAH'S BEING EXTREMELY
PLEASED WITH HERSELF.

1076
00:37:04,093 --> 00:37:05,595
SHE'S SLIPPING WEEK BY WEEK
FOR ME.

1077
00:37:05,595 --> 00:37:07,063
SHE'S GETTING
A LITTLE TOO ELEPHANT FOR ME.

1078
00:37:07,063 --> 00:37:08,631
- SHE'S OUT.
- TAKES ONE TO KNOW ONE.

1079
00:37:08,631 --> 00:37:10,166
THANK YOU. PROUD OF IT.

1080
00:37:14,170 --> 00:37:16,339
SIX BEAUTIFUL LADIES
STAND BEFORE ME,

1081
00:37:16,339 --> 00:37:19,809
BUT UNFORTUNATELY ONE OF YOU
HAS TO GO HOME TONIGHT.

1082
00:37:19,809 --> 00:37:21,911
THE FIRST NAME
THAT I'M GOING TO CALL...

1083
00:37:24,047 --> 00:37:26,149
KAHLEN.

1084
00:37:26,149 --> 00:37:28,985
WHO IS THIS GIRL STANDING
IN FRONT OF ME THIS WEEK?

1085
00:37:28,985 --> 00:37:30,520
I DON'T RECOGNIZE HER.

1086
00:37:30,520 --> 00:37:32,655
YOU MAY HAVE BEEN
A SPRINGBOK THIS WEEK,

1087
00:37:32,655 --> 00:37:34,624
BUT YOU'RE THE LION.

1088
00:37:34,624 --> 00:37:35,625
CONGRATULATIONS.

1089
00:37:35,625 --> 00:37:36,426
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING

1090
00:37:36,426 --> 00:37:38,194
TOWARDS BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

1091
00:37:38,194 --> 00:37:39,295
THANK YOU.

1092
00:37:39,295 --> 00:37:41,064
THE NEXT NAME
THAT I'M GOING TO CALL...

1093
00:37:44,033 --> 00:37:45,835
CHRISTINA.

1094
00:37:45,835 --> 00:37:48,204
CHRISTINA, YOU LEARNED TODAY
THAT EVERY MODEL,

1095
00:37:48,204 --> 00:37:52,175
AS YOU KNOW, HAS FLAWS,
AND EVERYBODY HAS TRICKS.

1096
00:37:52,175 --> 00:37:54,577
YOU LEARNED
A NEW TRICK TODAY.

1097
00:37:54,577 --> 00:37:55,578
CONGRATULATIONS.

1098
00:37:55,578 --> 00:37:56,646
THANK YOU.

1099
00:37:59,315 --> 00:38:00,383
NAIMA.

1100
00:38:02,452 --> 00:38:05,588
I'M GONNA BE
REALLY HONEST WITH YOU.

1101
00:38:05,588 --> 00:38:07,557
TODAY I WAS DRIVING UP
TO THIS JUDGING,

1102
00:38:07,557 --> 00:38:08,858
AND I WENT THROUGH
ALL THE GIRLS,

1103
00:38:08,858 --> 00:38:11,494
AND FOR SOME REASON,
I FORGOT ABOUT NAIMA

1104
00:38:11,494 --> 00:38:14,330
'CAUSE NAIMA'S PERSONALITY
DOESN'T POP.

1105
00:38:14,330 --> 00:38:16,065
IT DOESN'T MAKE ME
REMEMBER YOU

1106
00:38:16,065 --> 00:38:17,934
WHEN I GO HOME AT NIGHT
AND GO TO SLEEP

1107
00:38:17,934 --> 00:38:19,736
AND THINK ABOUT THE GIRLS.

1108
00:38:19,736 --> 00:38:22,238
I KNOW THERE'S SOMETHING IN YOU
THAT IS SO BEAUTIFUL,

1109
00:38:22,238 --> 00:38:24,907
AND I FEEL LIKE
YOU'RE STIFLING IT.

1110
00:38:24,907 --> 00:38:25,975
THANK YOU.

1111
00:38:30,480 --> 00:38:31,514
BRITTANY.

1112
00:38:35,351 --> 00:38:37,286
BRITTANY, YOU HAVE
THIS BEAUTIFUL,

1113
00:38:37,286 --> 00:38:39,022
EFFERVESCENT PERSONALITY,

1114
00:38:39,022 --> 00:38:40,857
BUT FROM WEEK TO WEEK,
YOUR TESTS--

1115
00:38:40,857 --> 00:38:42,792
YOU'RE JUST FALLING APART.

1116
00:38:42,792 --> 00:38:45,161
YOU HAVE TO USE
YOUR STRENGTH

1117
00:38:45,161 --> 00:38:46,929
TO GET TO THE HEAD
OF THIS PACK.

1118
00:38:46,929 --> 00:38:48,097
CONGRATULATIONS.

1119
00:38:52,135 --> 00:38:54,237
WILL KEENYAH AND MICHELLE
PLEASE STEP FORWARD?

1120
00:38:56,639 --> 00:38:58,875
I ONLY HAVE ONE PHOTO
IN MY HANDS,

1121
00:38:58,875 --> 00:39:00,009
AND THIS PHOTO REPRESENTS

1122
00:39:00,009 --> 00:39:01,878
THE GIRL THAT WILL STILL BE
IN THE RUNNING

1123
00:39:01,878 --> 00:39:04,147
TOWARDS BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

1124
00:39:04,147 --> 00:39:06,983
I WILL ONLY CALL ONE NAME.

1125
00:39:06,983 --> 00:39:08,217
THE GIRL THAT I DO NOT CALL

1126
00:39:08,217 --> 00:39:12,522
MUST IMMEDIATELY PACK HER BAGS
AND RETURN HOME.

1127
00:39:12,522 --> 00:39:14,690
TWO OF YOU HAVE
VERY DIFFERENT STRENGTHS.

1128
00:39:14,690 --> 00:39:17,460
MICHELLE, YOU HAVE A FACE
THAT IS RARE,

1129
00:39:17,460 --> 00:39:19,762
BUT YOU FALL APART
UNDER PRESSURE,

1130
00:39:19,762 --> 00:39:20,963
AND BEING A TOP MODEL

1131
00:39:20,963 --> 00:39:23,499
MEANS BEING UNDER PRESSURE
CONSTANTLY,

1132
00:39:23,499 --> 00:39:26,502
BEING SCRUTINIZED,
BROKEN DOWN AND PICKED APART.

1133
00:39:26,502 --> 00:39:28,471
WE'RE NOT SURE IF YOU'RE
STRONG ENOUGH FOR THAT.

1134
00:39:30,039 --> 00:39:31,808
KEENYAH,
WHEN WE LOOK AT YOU,

1135
00:39:31,808 --> 00:39:33,076
WE DON'T SEE A MODEL,

1136
00:39:33,076 --> 00:39:36,612
AND AS MUCH AS I HATE
AND PREACH ABOUT MODELS

1137
00:39:36,612 --> 00:39:37,880
NOT HAVING TO BE
STICK-SKINNY,

1138
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:41,050
WE HAVE TO FACE IT THAT
WE ARE IN THE FASHION INDUSTRY.

1139
00:39:41,050 --> 00:39:44,320
IF YOU DON'T FIT THE CLOTHES,
YOU DON'T WORK.

1140
00:39:44,320 --> 00:39:47,356
BOTH OF YOU GUYS' WEAKNESS--
I DON'T THINK THERE'S TIME

1141
00:39:47,356 --> 00:39:49,725
FOR EITHER OF YOU
TO OVERCOME THEM.

1142
00:39:49,725 --> 00:39:52,495
BUT WE'VE BEEN IN
THIS INDUSTRY FOR A LONG TIME,

1143
00:39:52,495 --> 00:39:54,630
AND THESE JUDGES HAVE
SEEN MIRACLES HAPPEN.

1144
00:39:59,335 --> 00:40:00,436
KEENYAH.

1145
00:40:09,045 --> 00:40:10,980
- CONGRATULATIONS.
- THANK YOU.

1146
00:40:10,980 --> 00:40:12,315
YOU'RE GONNA WORK
ON YOURSELF?

1147
00:40:12,315 --> 00:40:15,651
GET IT TOGETHER?
BUT HEALTHY.

1148
00:40:15,651 --> 00:40:16,586
YOU'RE STILL IN THE RUNNING

1149
00:40:16,586 --> 00:40:18,855
TOWARDS BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

1150
00:40:18,855 --> 00:40:19,822
THANK YOU.

1151
00:40:20,857 --> 00:40:22,425
THANK YOU, MICHELLE.

1152
00:40:22,425 --> 00:40:23,526
THANK YOU.

1153
00:40:23,526 --> 00:40:25,061
(sobbing)

1154
00:40:28,731 --> 00:40:30,399
THANK YOU, GUYS, SO MUCH.

1155
00:40:30,399 --> 00:40:31,901
I APPRECIATE IT.
THANK YOU.

1156
00:40:31,901 --> 00:40:33,202
ROCK 'EM HARD.

1157
00:40:33,202 --> 00:40:34,537
YOUR TIME WILL COME,
SWEETIE.

1158
00:40:38,107 --> 00:40:41,010
I WANTED THIS MORE
THAN ANYTHING IN THE WORLD.

1159
00:40:41,010 --> 00:40:42,745
I CAN'T EVEN,
LIKE, EXPLAIN

1160
00:40:42,745 --> 00:40:46,382
HOW MUCH I WANTED TO
BE UP THERE, BE NUMBER ONE,

1161
00:40:46,382 --> 00:40:47,517
BE THE BEST.

1162
00:40:50,553 --> 00:40:53,589
WHEN I CAME IN HERE,
I WAS EVEN MORE SHY AND TIMID,

1163
00:40:53,589 --> 00:40:56,159
AND THE ADVICE I HAVE GOTTEN

1164
00:40:56,159 --> 00:40:57,927
AND THE CRITICISM
I HAVE GOTTEN

1165
00:40:57,927 --> 00:40:59,729
HAS HELPED ME CHANGE,
DEFINITELY.

1166
00:41:02,532 --> 00:41:04,233
I'VE JUST BECOME
MORE CONFIDENT,

1167
00:41:04,233 --> 00:41:08,871
AND I ACTUALLY--
I FEEL BEAUTIFUL.

1168
00:41:08,871 --> 00:41:12,041
I DON'T THINK I'VE EVER
TRULY FELT THAT BEFORE.

1169
00:41:31,427 --> 00:41:34,096
STAY TUNED FOR SCENES
FROM OUR NEXT EPISODE.

1170
00:41:36,966 --> 00:41:39,268
COMING UP ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"--

1171
00:41:39,268 --> 00:41:42,004
THE GIRLS RACE TO IMPRESS
SOUTH AFRICA'S FASHION ELITE,

1172
00:41:42,004 --> 00:41:44,540
WHICH BRINGS OUT
KEENYAH'S COMPETITIVE SIDE.

1173
00:41:44,540 --> 00:41:45,308
CHEATER!

1174
00:41:45,308 --> 00:41:46,742
BUT ALL THEIR CLAWS
COME OUT

1175
00:41:46,742 --> 00:41:47,910
WHEN THE GIRLS
HAVE TO CRITIQUE

1176
00:41:47,910 --> 00:41:49,779
EACH OTHER'S PHOTOS
